Bot \u003crelease+l10nbumper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nfy-NL -\u003e e76aac6f79c8\nhe -\u003e 906ed6dde59c\nhu -\u003e a8761bcf302c\nnb-NO -\u003e 61d5fbf22298\nnl -\u003e 64abfab2deb6", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "423bb41c1a1c8f9557edb2e3e2ac9479aaae32ba", "parents": ["21900b4d869ee344259d49a84bbf5568b54e1b02"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566374429, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "251": {"changesets": [{"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573648 - Introduce ToDoubleAllowTrailingChars and ToFloatAllowTrailingChars. r=njn a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42239", "files": ["xpcom/string/nsStringObsolete.cpp", "xpcom/string/nsTString.h", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestStrings.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b2e95f71010d3ffa16c546805d130e86aec5957d", "parents": ["423bb41c1a1c8f9557edb2e3e2ac9479aaae32ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573648 - Use ToFloatAllowTrailingChars for parsing scale values in meta viewport tag. r=botond a=RyanVM\n\nFrom the spec \u003chttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-device-adapt/#parsing-algorithm\u003e\n\n  If a prefix of property-value can be converted to a number using strtod,\n  the value will be that number. The remainder of the string is ignored.\n\nNote that nsTSubStrubg::ToInteger() allows trailing characters as it is so that\nwe don't need to modify the width/height parser for meta viewport.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42240", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/test/mochitest.ini", "dom/base/test/test_meta_viewport_initial_scale_with_trailing_characters.html", "dom/base/test/test_meta_viewport_width_with_trailing_characters.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "24da9c922e80149648db905953aecc2a0a43d47a", "parents": ["b2e95f71010d3ffa16c546805d130e86aec5957d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573051 - Use both SHParseDisplayName and CreateUri to validate a uri. r=aklotz a=RyanVM\n\nFor launching with an external protocol handler on Windows, we validate a uri\nbefore sending it to `ShellExecute`, by converting a string into `PIDL` using\n`SHParseDisplayName` and extract a string back from PIDL using\n`IShellFolder::GetDisplayNameOf`.  The problem was that if a fragment, a\nstring following a hash mark (#), is always dropped after this validation.\nThis is caused by the intended design of Windows.\n\nA proposed fix is to use `CreateUri` for validation, which is used behind\n`IShellFolder::GetDisplayNameOf`.  However, we also keep `SHParseDisplayName`\nbecause there are cases where `CreateUri` succeeds while `SHParseDisplayName`\nfails such as a non-existent `file:` uri and we want to keep the same\nvalidation result for those cases.\n\nAdding `CreateUri` broke MinGW build because of our toolkit issue.  We use\ndynamic linking for MinGW build in the meantime.\n\nThis patch adds a new unittest to make sure the new validation logic\nbehaves the same as the old one except the fragment issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42041", "files": ["testing/cppunittest.ini", "toolkit/library/moz.build", "uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.cpp", "widget/windows/ShellHeaderOnlyUtils.h", "widget/windows/UrlmonHeaderOnlyUtils.h", "widget/windows/moz.build", "widget/windows/tests/TestUriValidation.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/TestUrisToValidate.h", "widget/windows/tests/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "19d213ec90fd9a919814724cadc8434ba0804997", "parents": ["24da9c922e80149648db905953aecc2a0a43d47a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1571081 - Make MediaKeys correctly specify a NS_INTERFACE_MAP_ENTRY for nsISupports. r=mccr8 a=RyanVM\n\nBug 1522547 overlooked the need for specifying map entries for both nsISupports\nand nsIDocumentActivity and only had the latter. This changeset adds the missing\nnsISupports case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42563", "files": ["dom/media/eme/MediaKeys.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "354369dda26e3f4906965471279a429278869c54", "parents": ["19d213ec90fd9a919814724cadc8434ba0804997"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566381610, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "252": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003carchaeopteryx@coole-files.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 19d213ec90fd (bug 1573051) for build bustage on Windows. a=backout", "files": ["testing/cppunittest.ini", "toolkit/library/moz.build", "uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.cpp", "widget/windows/ShellHeaderOnlyUtils.h", "widget/windows/UrlmonHeaderOnlyUtils.h", "widget/windows/moz.build", "widget/windows/tests/TestUriValidation.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/TestUrisToValidate.h", "widget/windows/tests/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aa8b14959979bbd03026ce6d4450fed5ca32cda5", "parents": ["354369dda26e3f4906965471279a429278869c54"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566387272, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "253": {"changesets": [{"author": "L10n Bumper Bot \u003crelease+l10nbumper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nbr -\u003e 64c36445645f\ncy -\u003e 1b9e944f37f5\ndsb -\u003e ee1d47f04f07\nes-ES -\u003e dd46a1c85278\nfr -\u003e 6878c4e51516\ngn -\u003e 8ced7dbc0005\nhsb -\u003e 8e5b3f80dff0\nhu -\u003e dd44c146951d\nit -\u003e 9db7e98fdfff\npt-BR -\u003e 3697e7f211a4\nro -\u003e 52296d14daac\nuk -\u003e 502d6e23d3a3\nzh-CN -\u003e 178364c883f9", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0bacd4cda626f3fe20fff96c5102e9bead4d32ee", "parents": ["aa8b14959979bbd03026ce6d4450fed5ca32cda5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566392428, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "254": {"changesets": [{"author": "L10n Bumper Bot \u003crelease+l10nbumper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nes-AR -\u003e 39cf4ec0b778\nes-MX -\u003e 0b424422a300\ngn -\u003e 79352757dec1\npl -\u003e 99679096f2e8\nro -\u003e 835c52c9c6c7\ntr -\u003e 2c5ddacf96f6", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4db0780028ae2119484aacc2375607062d45ed0b", "parents": ["0bacd4cda626f3fe20fff96c5102e9bead4d32ee"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566403257, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "255": {"changesets": [{"author": "Johann Hofmann \u003cjhofmann@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1568108 - Indent popup sub-item in the identity popup. r=pbz, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D38959", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteIdentity.js", "browser/themes/shared/notification-icons.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "698d088d135c9d0e4a1635f7c4745ee55f546d24", "parents": ["4db0780028ae2119484aacc2375607062d45ed0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1568047. r=froydnj a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D41466", "files": ["ipc/ipdl/ipdl/lower.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "134cc7161f236e02dc9e1f2a068c5182c413e531", "parents": ["698d088d135c9d0e4a1635f7c4745ee55f546d24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1571283 - Add null check for mObserver r=baku a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42092", "files": ["dom/fetch/FetchDriver.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5386529d27f4f2f9ce53a042ec82439c84c90052", "parents": ["134cc7161f236e02dc9e1f2a068c5182c413e531"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Robert Helmer \u003crhelmer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573285 - set system add-on enable pref on by default for Fennec r=snorp a=RyanVM\n\nThis was originally added in bug 1428459 to separate system add-on updates from app updates, but the pref only made it to desktop and not mobile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D41795", "files": ["mobile/android/app/mobile.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "18bcc03292a53b74e7e08c8534563da4b9075cbf", "parents": ["5386529d27f4f2f9ce53a042ec82439c84c90052"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vlad Baicu \u003cvlad.baicu@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573868 - Upload Mobile activation ping in onStart. r=nalexander a=RyanVM\n\nBug 1534451 added a non-trivial amount of background computation during\nonCreate. This introduced regressions by tickling the balance of existing\nrace conditions.\n\nWe're changing this by now uploading in onStart. Ideally we want to send\nthis mobile activation ping at least once from every client at startup. This change\nshould have minimal impact and keep the same consistency with the core ping.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D41980", "files": ["mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/telemetry/TelemetryActivationPingDelegate.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "71bdd4abde0d1b05c94b1bec4cf028a8bb242b91", "parents": ["18bcc03292a53b74e7e08c8534563da4b9075cbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573458 - Leave the atoms zone when performing a GC r=tcampbell a=RyanVM\n\nEntering the atoms zone with AutoAllocInAtomsZone is a bit of a special case and we don't support entering another realm in this state. Unfortunately this can happen during GC in a couple of place. The patch temporarily leaves the atoms zone during GC so that callbacks can enter whatever zones they like.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42312", "files": ["js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp", "js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-1573458.js", "js/src/vm/Realm.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5f5dadd6b749b1dca8e2299af7d6671d7c8a5620", "parents": ["71bdd4abde0d1b05c94b1bec4cf028a8bb242b91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573051 - Use both SHParseDisplayName and CreateUri to validate a uri. r=aklotz, a=RyanVM\n\nFor launching with an external protocol handler on Windows, we validate a uri\nbefore sending it to `ShellExecute`, by converting a string into `PIDL` using\n`SHParseDisplayName` and extract a string back from PIDL using\n`IShellFolder::GetDisplayNameOf`.  The problem was that if a fragment, a\nstring following a hash mark (#), is always dropped after this validation.\nThis is caused by the intended design of Windows.\n\nA proposed fix is to use `CreateUri` for validation, which is used behind\n`IShellFolder::GetDisplayNameOf`.  However, we also keep `SHParseDisplayName`\nbecause there are cases where `CreateUri` succeeds while `SHParseDisplayName`\nfails such as a non-existent `file:` uri and we want to keep the same\nvalidation result for those cases.\n\nAdding `CreateUri` broke MinGW build because of our toolkit issue.  We use\ndynamic linking for MinGW build in the meantime.\n\nThis patch adds a new unittest to make sure the new validation logic\nbehaves the same as the old one except the fragment issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42943", "files": ["testing/cppunittest.ini", "toolkit/library/moz.build", "uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.cpp", "widget/windows/ShellHeaderOnlyUtils.h", "widget/windows/UrlmonHeaderOnlyUtils.h", "widget/windows/moz.build", "widget/windows/tests/TestUriValidation.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/TestUrisToValidate.h", "widget/windows/tests/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "db930b04d9dc1760110b3957e48cd58bcb0be125", "parents": ["5f5dadd6b749b1dca8e2299af7d6671d7c8a5620"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1574972 - Make nsJSUtils::GetCallingLocation() fallible. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nSome German web sites seem to have started to have file names with\nhundreds of thousands of bytes long, which is causing OOM crashes on\nAndroid.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42674", "files": ["dom/base/nsJSUtils.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "41758ec7e4efa186b56bf0c27ed02cdd86b24a16", "parents": ["db930b04d9dc1760110b3957e48cd58bcb0be125"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1572838 - ensure osint commandline args are passed appropriately, r=mhowell,mossop a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42311", "files": ["browser/app/winlauncher/LauncherProcessWin.cpp", "toolkit/profile/nsToolkitProfileService.cpp", "toolkit/xre/CmdLineAndEnvUtils.h", "toolkit/xre/SafeMode.h", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "01f6b1c6b4dc8a54b20ff64c578747a753045c7c", "parents": ["41758ec7e4efa186b56bf0c27ed02cdd86b24a16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1572838 - stop processing osint in BrowserContentHandler.jsm, r=mossop a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D42311\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42580", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8b4ed9c4a3cb0598d10baaee12353f81e54a7c0c", "parents": ["01f6b1c6b4dc8a54b20ff64c578747a753045c7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ashley Rose \u003cashleyrose@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1574028: Fix ColorStateLists on Android Q r=petru a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42703", "files": ["mobile/android/app/src/main/res/color/pressed_about_page_header_grey.xml", "mobile/android/app/src/main/res/color/recyclerview_selector.xml", "mobile/android/app/src/main/res/color/state_pressed_toolbar_grey_pressed.xml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d574e9e14ca210c752f005fb2b55af3f79a03c9d", "parents": ["8b4ed9c4a3cb0598d10baaee12353f81e54a7c0c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566429991, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "256": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr68 repo-update HSTS HPKP blocklist remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43053", "files": ["browser/app/blocklist.xml", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2f3c8f7d6c5c296bd53f293336010214d0966290", "parents": ["d574e9e14ca210c752f005fb2b55af3f79a03c9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1575415 - Always register the nsApplicationChooser component in Gtk builds. r=froydnj, a=jcristau\n\nBug 1278282 removed Gtk2 support, so MOZ_WIDGET_TOOLKIT is always \"gtk3\"\nfor Gtk builds, and never \"gtk\", which makes the current check never\nmatch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42761", "files": ["widget/gtk/components.conf"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8e5270f2247bbdf9d7d11438e2e8b0b103294316", "parents": ["2f3c8f7d6c5c296bd53f293336010214d0966290"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kirk Steuber \u003cksteuber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1551913 - Fix issues setting update directory permissions. r=rstrong, a=jcristau\n\nThis patch addresses both Bug 1551913 and Bug 1552206.\n\nThis patches the update directory permission-fixing code.\n\nThis also fixes a related bug that I discovered while testing this patch: nsAutoSid doesn't actually work because both PSID and HANDLE are both typedef'ed from void*, so the compiler can't actually tell the difference between them and ends up calling CloseHandle instead of FreeSid. To fix this, I removed nsAutoSid and replaced it with UniqueSidPtr, a UniquePtr type that uses a custom deleter class to free the SID properly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D34941\n\n***\nBug 1570396 - Fix misc. issues with permission setting r=mhowell\n\nThis patch fixes a number of miscellaneous issues with permission setting.\nWhen we move a directory, recreate it, and move the contents back, those contents may be in use (possibly by antivirus). To address this, we now fall back to copying the data back and removing the originals.\n\nThe maximum number of backups to make when moving conflicting files is now 3 instead of 9. 9 seemed a bit excessive.\n\nThere is now an additional level of SetPermissionsOf, FilesAndDirsWithBadPerms. This new value causes permissions not to be fixed if we are unable to read them. This should prevent unnecessary permission fixes while still allowing us to aggressively set them when necessary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42066\n\n***\nBug 1486637 - Backout bug 1486637 and related patches. r=agashlin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42143", "files": ["toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/moz.build", "toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/serviceinstall.cpp", "toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/usertoken.cpp", "toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/usertoken.h", "toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/workmonitor.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/commonupdatedir.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/commonupdatedir.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatedefines.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatehelper.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatehelper.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatererrors.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updateutils_win.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updateutils_win.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/win_dirent.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/win_dirent.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_base_updater/invalidArgInstallDirPathTooLongFailure.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_base_updater/invalidArgInstallDirPathTraversalFailure.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_base_updater/invalidArgInstallWorkingDirPathNotSameFailure_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_base_updater/invalidArgStageDirNotInInstallDirFailure_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_base_updater/invalidArgWorkingDirPathLocalUNCFailure_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_base_updater/invalidArgWorkingDirPathRelativeFailure.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_service_updater/invalidArgInstallDirPathTooLongFailureSvc.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_service_updater/invalidArgInstallDirPathTraversalFailureSvc.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_service_updater/invalidArgInstallWorkingDirPathNotSameFailureSvc_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_service_updater/invalidArgStageDirNotInInstallDirFailureSvc_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_service_updater/invalidArgWorkingDirPathLocalUNCFailureSvc_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_service_updater/invalidArgWorkingDirPathRelativeFailureSvc.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp", "toolkit/xre/moz.build", "xpcom/base/nsWindowsHelpers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "35a6d667978cfb807610e11b84fd126891bfcc7e", "parents": ["8e5270f2247bbdf9d7d11438e2e8b0b103294316"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566485896, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "257": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1571120 - Check for file paths before assuming a URL. r=aswan a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D41255", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/policytest_v0.1.xpi", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensions.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "26153798092d0e63038f5fe8fab927dbd87c25b8", "parents": ["35a6d667978cfb807610e11b84fd126891bfcc7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1571033 - Don't clear user homepage when setting default via policy. r=mconley a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D40453", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_set_homepage.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b392c57375cc4d7482a8bfa3b8e34da8315921e6", "parents": ["26153798092d0e63038f5fe8fab927dbd87c25b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1547977 - Use JS::DefaultHeapMaxBytes instead of 4 MB for PAC runtime. r=jonco,mayhemer a=jcristau\n\nDefaultHeapMaxBytes is currently 32 MB so it should give us a bit more breathing\nroom.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42819", "files": ["netwerk/base/ProxyAutoConfig.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "de19545f3c19929655604b24b1f2d10e618e91bb", "parents": ["b392c57375cc4d7482a8bfa3b8e34da8315921e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Haik Aftandilian \u003chaftandilian@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1558924 - [10.15] Widevine crashes on macOS Catalina Beta r=handyman a=jcristau\n\nAllow limited access to the proc_pidinfo() syscall from the GMP sandbox.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36810", "files": ["security/sandbox/mac/SandboxPolicyGMP.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4f6134ab70f2428f6f5f9abb5e578061e35fe04c", "parents": ["de19545f3c19929655604b24b1f2d10e618e91bb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566487507, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "csabou@mozilla.com"}, "258": {"changesets": [{"author": "Haik Aftandilian \u003chaftandilian@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1570581 - Starting with Firefox 68.0.1, Adobe Acrobat Extension for Firefox fails to send apple events to target application (Acrobat) r=handyman a=RyanVM\n\nRelax our Hardened Runtime settings to allow the com.apple.security.automation.apple-events entitlement so that native messaging webextension helper apps (which are launched by and are child processes of Firefox) can use Apple Events to signal other processes. This will apply to Firefox and all child processes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42929", "files": ["security/mac/hardenedruntime/developer.entitlements.xml", "security/mac/hardenedruntime/production.entitlements.xml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3074c5a47ad5037b19a52fca06c202add0169915", "parents": ["4f6134ab70f2428f6f5f9abb5e578061e35fe04c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566508983, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "259": {"changesets": [{"author": "L10n Bumper Bot \u003crelease+l10nbumper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nit -\u003e 332f86817761", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "383ff40df7c5f34da231dba211df306d501a9ee4", "parents": ["3074c5a47ad5037b19a52fca06c202add0169915"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566547233, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "260": {"changesets": [{"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1570358: Check validity of enums before playing back Moz2D RecordedEvents. r=jrmuizel a=jcristau", "files": ["gfx/2d/InlineTranslator.cpp", "gfx/2d/Logging.h", "gfx/2d/RecordedEvent.cpp", "gfx/2d/RecordedEvent.h", "gfx/2d/RecordedEventImpl.h", "gfx/2d/RecordingTypes.h", "layout/printing/DrawEventRecorder.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "26b6bb71abca805d8f7c97b2bdda8d648efc074c", "parents": ["383ff40df7c5f34da231dba211df306d501a9ee4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1282776 - Finalize crash reports for child process crashes happening too early r=froydnj a=RyanVM\n\nThis changes the way crash reports for child processes happening too early\nduring the child process' startup. Before bug 1547698 we wrote a partial\n.extra file with those crashes that lacked the process type. The user would\nnot be notified of those crashes until she restarted Firefox and even when\nsubmitted those crashes would be erroneously labeled as browser crashes.\n\nAfter bug 1547698 we stopped writing .extra files entirely for those crashes\nwhich left orphaned .dmp files among the pending crash reports.\n\nThis patch does three things to improve the situation:\n\n* It writes a partial .extra file so that the crashes are detected at the next\n  startup. So the user is still not notified directly of these crashes but she\n  can report them later.\n* It adds the process type to the .extra file so that the crash reporters are\n  labelled correctly.\n* It fixes a leak in the `pidToMinidump` hash-map. Since the crashes were\n  not finalized the `ChildProcessData` strucutre associated with them would\n  never be fred.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D40810", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.h", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.cpp", "dom/plugins/ipc/PluginModuleParent.cpp", "dom/plugins/ipc/PluginModuleParent.h", "gfx/ipc/GPUChild.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRChild.cpp", "ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/src/remotesandboxbroker/RemoteSandboxBrokerParent.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsDummyExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsExceptionHandler.h", "toolkit/xre/nsEmbedFunctions.cpp", "xpcom/build/nsXULAppAPI.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b0081b2c868092660d1a649f385ed481d0bbe249", "parents": ["26b6bb71abca805d8f7c97b2bdda8d648efc074c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1571682 - Make allocationSiteGroup fail cleanly on OOM. r=tcampbell,jandem, a=jcristau\n\nThis should make this fail cleanly on OOM rather than crashing, which should make this crash go away (without reducing memory usage obviously). The problem was the lack of hasHash/ensureHash methods that we use to handle OOM when generating unique IDs for GC things. I also tidied the equivalent code for ObjectGroupRealm::NewEntry (FallibleHashMethods is already implemented for MovableCellHasher).\n\nWe could further improve this by giving each script an immutable hash code on creation if you think it's worth the tradeoff of storing this for every script.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D41233", "files": ["js/src/vm/ObjectGroup.cpp", "js/src/vm/ObjectGroup.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a975570ee8f162255faf10d36e11eb5373bf0ecb", "parents": ["b0081b2c868092660d1a649f385ed481d0bbe249"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Haik Aftandilian \u003chaftandilian@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1562684 - PR_GetLibraryFilePathname is returning absolute paths in MacOS Catalina r=froydnj a=RyanVM\n\nInstead of using symlinks, copy .dylib files to the ${OBJDIR}/dist/Nightly{Debug}.app/Contents/MacOS dir for local builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D41926", "files": ["browser/app/Makefile.in", "browser/app/macbuild/Contents/MacOS-files-copy.in", "browser/app/macbuild/Contents/MacOS-files.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "412e4ecdf016103628eae85871108c1c830f48ef", "parents": ["a975570ee8f162255faf10d36e11eb5373bf0ecb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yaron Tausky \u003cytausky@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1544750 - Part 2: Refactor Key::EncodeJSValInternal to show direct correspondence to spec r=asuth,tcampbell a=RyanVM\n\nThis commit adds the text of the spec as inline comments and refactors\nthe code such that it directly corresponds to the spec's steps. This\nmakes it easier to understand how the spec's algorithm is implemented.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43016", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBCursor.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBFactory.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBKeyRange.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBResult.h", "dom/indexedDB/Key.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/Key.h", "dom/indexedDB/KeyPath.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/moz.build", "dom/indexedDB/test/gtest/TestIDBResult.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ebb385dc5c27434ca6e1b951fa57492bdc1e1d62", "parents": ["412e4ecdf016103628eae85871108c1c830f48ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Robert Strong \u003crobert.bugzilla@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1574980 - Fix issues with maintenance service install. r=bytesized a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43034", "files": ["toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/serviceinstall.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatehelper.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "091473bf2727d37a4107cfca1185ef99c3f2eeff", "parents": ["ebb385dc5c27434ca6e1b951fa57492bdc1e1d62"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566589678, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "261": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003carchaeopteryx@coole-files.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset ebb385dc5c27 (bug 1544750) for bustage in IDBResult.h. a=backout", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBCursor.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBFactory.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBKeyRange.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBResult.h", "dom/indexedDB/Key.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/Key.h", "dom/indexedDB/KeyPath.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/moz.build", "dom/indexedDB/test/gtest/TestIDBResult.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9fd0d4493c77bfed937299c2b7fd3843f8543a3a", "parents": ["091473bf2727d37a4107cfca1185ef99c3f2eeff"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566591148, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "262": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jorg K \u003cjorgk@jorgk.com\u003e", "branch": "THUNDERBIRD_68_VERBRANCH", "desc": "Backed out changeset 6d7610f4d26d (bug 1360603 for causing bug 1500895) to build Thunderbird 68.0. a=jorgk DONTBUILD", "files": ["toolkit/content/contentAreaUtils.js", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_saveImageURL.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2f459603370d1d35a56ca4e9cee21f7766bbb832", "parents": ["0d2d8881be5ea5d83959650122af2c355a360549"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566718870, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "mozilla@jorgk.com"}, "263": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr68 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43437", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5ebfac7c21193aea32d64d3c9573001e480e620d", "parents": ["9fd0d4493c77bfed937299c2b7fd3843f8543a3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "T\u0133l Coosemans \u003ctijl@FreeBSD.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1575876 - Drop header unused on FreeBSD that breaks with new libc++. r=bwc, a=RyanVM", "files": ["media/mtransport/third_party/nICEr/src/stun/stun.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9eaf06067c90a1d5a63f97f5972ad031a23947d2", "parents": ["5ebfac7c21193aea32d64d3c9573001e480e620d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yaron Tausky \u003cytausky@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1554989 - Fix implicit checker on inheriting constructors. r=andi, a=RyanVM\n\nInheriting constructors are implicitly introduced via a using-declaration.\nSince the C++ grammar doesn't allow attributes on using-declarations, it\nis currently impossible to add MOZ_IMPLICIT to implicit inheriting\nconstructors.\n\nThis commit changes the AST matcher such that it ignores inheriting\nconstructors altogether. If they are inheriting from an implicit inherited\nconstructor, that constructor's check should be enough to ensure that no\nconstructors are unintentionally implicit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43434", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/CustomMatchers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f635742506afeb830819a9555a0776d0c6fd58d5", "parents": ["9eaf06067c90a1d5a63f97f5972ad031a23947d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yaron Tausky \u003cytausky@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1501152 - Refactor Key::EncodeJSValInternal to show direct correspondence to spec r=asuth,tcampbell a=RyanVM\n\nThis commit adds the text of the spec as inline comments and refactors\nthe code such that it directly corresponds to the spec's steps. This\nmakes it easier to understand how the spec's algorithm is implemented.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43016", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBCursor.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBFactory.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBKeyRange.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBResult.h", "dom/indexedDB/Key.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/Key.h", "dom/indexedDB/KeyPath.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/moz.build", "dom/indexedDB/test/gtest/TestIDBResult.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "80175938fbd8b80caa38609199f3b111bedc3aec", "parents": ["f635742506afeb830819a9555a0776d0c6fd58d5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1566825590, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "264": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1541344 - Delete plugin-data only for the sites with data. r=gsvelto, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D40644", "files": ["toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "455ea8f521c18812fdf486c68d24ffb63360f006", "parents": ["80175938fbd8b80caa38609199f3b111bedc3aec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brendan Dahl \u003cbdahl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1568071 - Add a way to disable external links in PDFS. r=yury, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D43140", "files": ["browser/extensions/pdfjs/README.mozilla", "browser/extensions/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.js", "browser/extensions/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.js", "browser/extensions/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "380fedbb18002297f1b233bd9c09764e59ddaa86", "parents": ["455ea8f521c18812fdf486c68d24ffb63360f006"], "tags": ["FENNEC_68_1b8_BUILD1", "FENNEC_68_1b8_RELEASE", "FIREFOX_68_1_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_68_1_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1566825987, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "46": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 501f4667334f5ccaee37ca013d6d1a5923e076f6 with FENNEC_68_0_BUILD3 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "55ad5032ff435232981629bea65d50544bf9a4fb", "parents": ["501f4667334f5ccaee37ca013d6d1a5923e076f6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562377473, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "47": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 501f4667334f5ccaee37ca013d6d1a5923e076f6 with FIREFOX_68_0esr_BUILD2 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c3e66e697e7f3a3d7c67d44620ff29245f7be5cd", "parents": ["55ad5032ff435232981629bea65d50544bf9a4fb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562377667, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "48": {"changesets": [{"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1564103 - Bump version.txt on Fennec Release r=RyanVM,Callek a=release\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D37246", "files": ["taskcluster/ci/release-version-bump/kind.yml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c1d92777ceb085a5b9bdea8c763ec4071ef52daf", "parents": ["c3e66e697e7f3a3d7c67d44620ff29245f7be5cd"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562595561, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "jlorenzo@mozilla.com"}, "49": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003crelease@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Update configs. IGNORE BROKEN CHANGESETS CLOSED TREE NO BUG a=release ba=release", "files": ["browser/config/version.txt", "browser/config/version_display.txt", "config/milestone.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "eaf43b44d96fb8505554b3ef6cbc20034e39f1fc", "parents": ["c1d92777ceb085a5b9bdea8c763ec4071ef52daf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562607992, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld-merge"}, "50": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Manually bump the Fennec version numbers. r=tomprince, a=release DONTBUILD", "files": ["mobile/android/config/version-files/beta/version.txt", "mobile/android/config/version-files/beta/version_display.txt", "mobile/android/config/version-files/nightly/version.txt", "mobile/android/config/version-files/nightly/version_display.txt", "mobile/android/config/version-files/release/version.txt", "mobile/android/config/version-files/release/version_display.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "58234632acb4ad83775d57cda4ca07e0be42c38f", "parents": ["eaf43b44d96fb8505554b3ef6cbc20034e39f1fc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562612417, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "51": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backout changeset e85578d93db4 (bug 1547565) for telemetry regression. a=RyanVM", "files": ["js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/vm/AtomsTable.h", "js/src/vm/JSAtom.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "98e0742f83444c9be7b3371d82d9e3031e10766a", "parents": ["58234632acb4ad83775d57cda4ca07e0be42c38f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1550105 - Implement the parser for scale values in viewport meta tag as what the spec defines. r=botond, a=RyanVM\n\nThe relevant definition in the spec;\n https://drafts.csswg.org/css-device-adapt/#min-scale-max-scale\n\nBefore this change, if both of initial-scale and maximum-scale are negative,\nboth values are clamped to 0.25. Whereas with this change, negative scale\nvalues are treated as if it's not specified so that initial-scale value is\nautomatically calculated based on the layout viewport size.\nnegative-initial-and-maximum-scale.html is a test case for the case.\n\nAlso with this change, initial-scale values are going to be clamped to the\nrange [0.25, 10] during parsing it so that initial-scale-0.html and\ninitial-scale-100.html need to be modified, now the former is scaled by 0.25x,\nthe latter is scaled by 10x.\n(Before this change, initial-scale=0 and initial-scale=100 were treated as\n invalid scale values in nsViewportInfo::ConstrainViewportValues[1])\n\n[1] https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/6c9f60f8cc064a1005cd8141ecd526578ae9da7a/dom/base/nsViewportInfo.cpp#15,19\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D32098", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/reftest/initial-scale-1-ref.html", "layout/reftests/meta-viewport/initial-scale-0.html", "layout/reftests/meta-viewport/initial-scale-10-ref.html", "layout/reftests/meta-viewport/initial-scale-100.html", "layout/reftests/meta-viewport/negative-initial-and-maximum-scale.html", "layout/reftests/meta-viewport/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fe659e4395fa4de3ebaee61ac3b085db882ecf62", "parents": ["98e0742f83444c9be7b3371d82d9e3031e10766a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1555511 Part 1: Make MVM::UpdateResolution clamp viewport zoom for the new display size later in the calculation. r=botond, a=RyanVM\n\nThe existing math is attempting to adjust the display scale ratio to\nprevent the new size from landing outside the min/max zoom bounds. This\nintroduces unwanted side effects that can be avoided by simply clamping\nto min/max at the end. The remaining math correctly handles the case\nwhere the zoom has ALREADY been clamped, which is the only important\ncase.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D32908", "files": ["layout/base/MobileViewportManager.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4eb8bea60c4dbe965e29dc6ee4fe6ea6c1c40556", "parents": ["fe659e4395fa4de3ebaee61ac3b085db882ecf62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1555511 Part 2: Remove a float division in MVM::ScaleZoomWithDisplayWidth. r=botond, a=RyanVM\n\nThis is a drive-by fix to turn a division into a multiplication. It also\nis more correct in that the existing code attempts a divide-by-zero if\naNewViewport.width is zero. The updated code will instead return a zoom\nof zero in such a case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D32909", "files": ["layout/base/MobileViewportManager.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "305d795fb86ea7ae4fb00f2b8154c40e2f564660", "parents": ["4eb8bea60c4dbe965e29dc6ee4fe6ea6c1c40556"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1555511 Part 3: Refactor viewport resize test helper functions. r=botond, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D33362", "files": ["devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/browser_viewport_resizing_fixed_width.js", "devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/browser_viewport_resizing_fixed_width_and_zoom.js", "devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/browser_viewport_resizing_scrollbar.js", "devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5eefd1eebf97eb15f0eca7fd56dab93858b980ee", "parents": ["305d795fb86ea7ae4fb00f2b8154c40e2f564660"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Werth \u003cbwerth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1555511 Part 4: Add a test of resizing a document with meta viewport minimum-scale. r=botond, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D33100", "files": ["devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/browser.ini", "devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/browser_viewport_resizing_minimum_scale.js", "devtools/client/responsive.html/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a80a09e9c87cdb203dc06e3a6a9925f5127dc680", "parents": ["5eefd1eebf97eb15f0eca7fd56dab93858b980ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Petru Lingurar \u003cpetru.lingurar@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1551614 - Call BrowserApp's onCreate() before finish(); r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nFix for the following scenario:\n- \"Don't keep activities\" checked\n- Change system language\n\nUpon detecting a locale change in BrowserApp's onCreate() we would call\nfinish() and then return before calling super.onCreate().\n\nThis patch introdues the call to super.onCreate() before returning and ensures\nthat the app will die cleanly so that upon restarting Gecko can reinit add-ons\nthat touch the UI.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D35402", "files": ["mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoApp.java", "mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/home/CombinedHistoryPanel.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "02da79cc95ddf4940780aa3353934f1895176a98", "parents": ["a80a09e9c87cdb203dc06e3a6a9925f5127dc680"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Petru Lingurar \u003cpetru.lingurar@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1551614 - Simpler way of restarting our app in a new process; r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nOur Restarter Service would have issues on Android Q:\nIt would run on a separate process that allowed it to kill the app's process\nbut when trying to restart the app it would fail because it would've been a\nbackground Service and as such it would've been restricted from starting other\nAndroid Application components.\n\nTo make it work on Android Q we would need to migrate it to a foreground\nservice or piggy-back the SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW permission given by the user for\nthe Tab Queue functionality.\n\nThe chosen solution is simpler and not affected by any of those limitations.\n\nDepends on D35402\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D35403", "files": ["mobile/android/base/AndroidManifest.xml.in", "mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoApplication.java", "mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/Restarter.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "feb6d47c83037c9992a9f3a5d5b5833bbe421e67", "parents": ["02da79cc95ddf4940780aa3353934f1895176a98"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562616112, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "52": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jeff Gilbert \u003cjgilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1544446 - Restrict macOS MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE to 8192. r=lsalzman, a=RyanVM\n\nAlso clean up MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE restriction code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36144", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLContext.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bf902a42a7c4cb97a94d9ebfbfdf822d43a737fd", "parents": ["feb6d47c83037c9992a9f3a5d5b5833bbe421e67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sotaro \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1546397 - Blacklist WebGL on some android devices. r=jgilbert, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36153", "files": ["widget/android/GfxInfo.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "184ed37f572082d368652049719e05309bc2c888", "parents": ["bf902a42a7c4cb97a94d9ebfbfdf822d43a737fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Arant \u003cbrad.arant@softvision.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1489458 - Remove extraneous console logging in browser.js. r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36284", "files": ["mobile/android/chrome/content/browser.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bff36fbf2628517deea3d764c89dbb5a245dbab9", "parents": ["184ed37f572082d368652049719e05309bc2c888"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kristen Wright \u003ckwright@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1544452 - Increase slack boundaries for ExpirationTracker gtest. r=froydnj, a=RyanVM\n\nIncreased slack boundaries to account for issues with timer bounds in macos 1014. Lower bound slack = 60ms and upper bound slack = 1200ms. The intent is to get gtests working in the short term while timer delays are fixed, then roll the slack boundary back to 30ms.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36419", "files": ["xpcom/tests/gtest/TestExpirationTracker.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "38b8cb9745e1974fcdd975c9bb41ff6ac23bf803", "parents": ["bff36fbf2628517deea3d764c89dbb5a245dbab9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron Kaiser \u003cspectre@floodgap.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1512162 - A better fix for incorrect code generation on ppc64le. r=bholley, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36439", "files": ["js/xpconnect/src/XPCWrappedNative.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "582e8db79ecc8b63f26dba6f59eb723f97ac79da", "parents": ["38b8cb9745e1974fcdd975c9bb41ff6ac23bf803"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alwu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1552818 - part1 : prevent to leak audio-playback notification. r=padenot, a=RyanVM\n\nThis test will leak one `audio-playback` notification to next test, because when we close this test, we would close iframe and send the `inaudible-pause` notification.\n\nIt would somehow affect the following test if the next one is also listening to the `audio-playback` notification.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36534", "files": ["dom/base/test/test_audioNotificationNavigationWebAudio.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0ddbde0b74fba2226258f381c94437782179068e", "parents": ["582e8db79ecc8b63f26dba6f59eb723f97ac79da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alwu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1552818 - part2 : refactor test 'test_audioNotificationNavigationWebAudio.html' by using async-await form. r=padenot. a=RyanVM\n\nUsing async and await form can increase the readability of the test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36535", "files": ["dom/base/test/test_audioNotificationNavigationWebAudio.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "16410020f7e1a7b8dd7922def256eae4e08d23be", "parents": ["0ddbde0b74fba2226258f381c94437782179068e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562616844, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "53": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nathan Froyd \u003cfroydnj@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1561410 - modify TestThreadPool to be more robust with bad timekeeping; r=KrisWright, a=RyanVM\n\nGiving each logical test its own counter variable will help tests to not\ninterfere with each other.  We also make one infinite looping thread\nexit so we're not chewing CPU after these tests finish.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36522", "files": ["xpcom/tests/gtest/TestThreadPool.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b63652f5efa0ab593d2ebb419d1758eb36000511", "parents": ["16410020f7e1a7b8dd7922def256eae4e08d23be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Gilbert \u003cjgilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1558339 - Clamp TEXTURE_[BASE,MAX]_LEVEL for drivers. r=lsalzman, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36672", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTexture.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d38a5b282a60c24ea3828efaf41b1898e59b4511", "parents": ["b63652f5efa0ab593d2ebb419d1758eb36000511"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1545429 - Avoid passing unsupported Android screen orientation flag combinations to Gecko. r=snorp, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36351", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoScreenOrientation.java", "widget/android/AndroidBridge.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3e87ad49a19b9da1a43fb9e8daf455d2315e28e2", "parents": ["d38a5b282a60c24ea3828efaf41b1898e59b4511"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edwin Gao \u003cegao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1562083 - explicitly insert sys.path to env for use in subprocess for python3 mozprocess unit tests. r=jmaher, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36681", "files": ["taskcluster/ci/source-test/python.yml", "taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/job/mach.py", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/tests/test_kill.py", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/tests/test_misc.py", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/tests/test_wait.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2a18a2cb9db864f72d4e1814b5e46dba3add7c07", "parents": ["3e87ad49a19b9da1a43fb9e8daf455d2315e28e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Petru Lingurar \u003cpetru.lingurar@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1562831 - Stop the Crash Service cleanly to prevent it's restart; r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nThe service would be restarted after System.exit(0) which would show the crash\nfeedback form again to the user.\n\nThat System.exit(0) was initially used to prevent a silent ANR because of the\nService being started from background on Android Oreo+ without a foreground\nnotification.\n\nTo overcome all this we'll also use a foreground notification on Android Oreo+\nbut with NotificationManager.IMPORTANCE_LOW to be non-intrusive.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36746", "files": ["mobile/android/base/AppConstants.java.in", "mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/CrashHandlerService.java", "mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/notifications/NotificationHelper.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "161aae250e42256d501e99f946e98d066dfb147f", "parents": ["2a18a2cb9db864f72d4e1814b5e46dba3add7c07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1562886 - Avoid noinline on GCC with skcms to work around compiler error. r=me, a=RyanVM", "files": ["gfx/skia/skia/third_party/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "420c07d42512ed9fd73d694d800752777650e78e", "parents": ["161aae250e42256d501e99f946e98d066dfb147f"], "tags": ["FENNEC_68_1b1_BUILD1"]}], "date": 1562617329, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "54": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 420c07d42512ed9fd73d694d800752777650e78e with FENNEC_68_1b1_BUILD1 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "59a3b58682a8a2de6bb29834d583d6e59bdf70f1", "parents": ["420c07d42512ed9fd73d694d800752777650e78e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562634131, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "55": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 501f4667334f5ccaee37ca013d6d1a5923e076f6 with FENNEC_68_0_RELEASE a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "17f67261f92b8d436dcd5a03379a0b61b306e6d6", "parents": ["59a3b58682a8a2de6bb29834d583d6e59bdf70f1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562676722, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "56": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 501f4667334f5ccaee37ca013d6d1a5923e076f6 with FIREFOX_68_0esr_RELEASE a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c25f826803a2962f95841d106331cbbb60214a78", "parents": ["17f67261f92b8d436dcd5a03379a0b61b306e6d6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1562677302, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "57": {"changesets": [{"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1561617 - part 1: Bump mozilla-version to 0.3.4 r=sfraser a=release\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D37395", "files": ["third_party/python/enum34/enum/doc/enum.pdf", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/PKG-INFO", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/balrog.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/gecko.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/maven.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/parser.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/test/__init__.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/test/test_balrog.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/test/test_gecko.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/test/test_maven.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/test/test_version.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/mozilla_version/version.py", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/requirements-coveralls.txt", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/requirements-docs.txt", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/requirements-test.txt", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/requirements.txt", "third_party/python/mozilla-version/version.txt", "third_party/python/psutil/psutil/_pslinux.py", "third_party/python/requirements.in", "third_party/python/requirements.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "df4b3bf7ac5b3c9a31e045c766560e31df4b730b", "parents": ["c25f826803a2962f95841d106331cbbb60214a78"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1561617 - part 2: Support bumping for Fennec on ESR r=sfraser a=release\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D37396", "files": ["testing/mozharness/configs/merge_day/bump_esr68.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/merge_day/gecko_migration.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "040ebb24b019a3934928a9dd7d5233cb64582aa9", "parents": ["df4b3bf7ac5b3c9a31e045c766560e31df4b730b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1561617 - part 3: push-apk-checks now accepts new version numbers r=sfraser a=release\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D37397", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/mozapkpublisher/Dockerfile"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1c870b90062317c12c62818e53cb77e508050e86", "parents": ["040ebb24b019a3934928a9dd7d5233cb64582aa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1561617 - part 4: `mach send-buglist-email` now accepts new version numbers r=sfraser a=release\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D37398", "files": ["python/mozrelease/mozrelease/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d2e9196354f90b8e21f6c4b7ad1e736aa63e7646", "parents": ["1c870b90062317c12c62818e53cb77e508050e86